{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P48454","secondaryAccessions":["B4DRT5","Q9BSS6","Q9H4M5"],"uniProtkbId":"PP2BC_HUMAN","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"1996-02-01","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2009-09-01","entryVersion":207,"sequenceVersion":3},"annotationScore":5,"organism":{"scientificName":"Homo sapiens","commonName":"Human","taxonId":9606,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Euarchontoglires","Primates","Haplorrhini","Catarrhini","Hominidae","Homo"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2B catalytic subunit gamma isoform"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19154138"}],"value":"3.1.3.16"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"CAM-PRP catalytic subunit"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Calcineurin, testis-specific catalytic subunit"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Calmodulin-dependent calcineurin A subunit gamma isoform"}}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"value":"PPP3CC"},"synonyms":[{"value":"CALNA3"},{"value":"CNA3"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19154138"}],"value":"Calcium-dependent, calmodulin-stimulated protein phosphatase which plays an essential role in the transduction of intracellular Ca(2+)-mediated signals. Dephosphorylates and activates transcription factor NFATC1. Dephosphorylates and inactivates transcription factor ELK1. Dephosphorylates DARPP32"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"O-phospho-L-seryl-[protein] + H2O = L-seryl-[protein] + phosphate","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:20629"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:9863"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:11604"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15377"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29999"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:43474"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:83421"}],"ecNumber":"3.1.3.16","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19154138"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"O-phospho-L-threonyl-[protein] + H2O = L-threonyl-[protein] + phosphate","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:47004"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:11060"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:11605"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15377"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30013"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:43474"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:61977"}],"ecNumber":"3.1.3.16","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19154138"}]}},{"commentType":"COFACTOR","cofactors":[{"name":"Fe(3+)","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P16298"}],"cofactorCrossReference":{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29034"}}],"note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P16298"}],"value":"Binds 1 Fe(3+) ion per subunit."}]}},{"commentType":"COFACTOR","cofactors":[{"name":"Zn(2+)","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P16298"}],"cofactorCrossReference":{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29105"}}],"note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P16298"}],"value":"Binds 1 zinc ion per subunit."}]}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P16298"}],"value":"Activated by Ca(2+)-bound calmodulin following an increase in intracellular Ca(2+). At low Ca(2+) concentrations, the catalytic subunit (also known as calcineurin A) is inactive and is bound to the regulatory subunit (also known as calcineurin B) in which only two high-affinity binding sites are occupied by Ca(2+). In response to elevated calcium levels, the occupancy of the low-affinity sites on calcineurin B by Ca(2+) causes a conformational change of the C-terminal regulatory domain of calcineurin A, resulting in the exposure of the calmodulin-binding domain and in the partial activation of calcineurin A. The subsequent binding of Ca(2+)-bound calmodulin leads to the displacement of the autoinhibitory domain from the active site and possibly of the autoinhibitory segment from the substrate binding site which fully activates calcineurin A"}],"commentType":"ACTIVITY REGULATION"},{"commentType":"BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES","kineticParameters":{"michaelisConstants":[{"constant":1.27,"unit":"uM","substrate":"NFATC1","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19154138"}]},{"constant":0.94,"unit":"uM","substrate":"DARPP32","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19154138"}]}]}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P16298"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P48455"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19154138"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"34446558"}],"value":"Forms a complex composed of a calmodulin-dependent catalytic subunit (also known as calcineurin A) and a regulatory Ca(2+)-binding subunit (also known as calcineurin B) (PubMed:19154138). There are three catalytic subunits, each encoded by a separate gene (PPP3CA, PPP3CB, and PPP3CC) and two regulatory subunits which are also encoded by separate genes (PPP3R1 and PPP3R2). In response to an increase in Ca(2+) intracellular levels, forms a complex composed of PPP3CC/calcineurin A, calcineurin B and calmodulin (By similarity). Interacts (via calmodulin-binding domain) with calmodulin; the interaction depends on calmodulin binding to Ca(2+) (By similarity). Interacts with UNC119 (By similarity). Interacts with SPATA33 (via PQIIIT motif) (PubMed:34446558). Interacts with VDAC2 in a SPATA33-dependent manner (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"INTERACTION","interactions":[{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P48454","intActId":"EBI-2827192"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P49418","geneName":"AMPH","intActId":"EBI-7121510"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P48454","intActId":"EBI-2827192"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P05067","geneName":"APP","intActId":"EBI-77613"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P48454","intActId":"EBI-2827192"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P63098","geneName":"PPP3R1","intActId":"EBI-915984"},"numberOfExperiments":7,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P48454","intActId":"EBI-2827192"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q96N06","geneName":"SPATA33","intActId":"EBI-17572815"},"numberOfExperiments":4,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P48454","intActId":"EBI-2827192"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q13432","geneName":"UNC119","intActId":"EBI-711260"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P48455"}],"value":"Localizes in the mitochondria in a SPATA33-dependent manner"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P48455"}],"value":"Mitochondrion","id":"SL-0173"}}]},{"commentType":"ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS","events":["Alternative splicing"],"isoforms":[{"name":{"value":"1"},"isoformIds":["P48454-1"],"isoformSequenceStatus":"Displayed"},{"name":{"value":"2"},"isoformIds":["P48454-2"],"sequenceIds":["VSP_037946"],"isoformSequenceStatus":"Described"},{"name":{"value":"3"},"isoformIds":["P48454-3"],"sequenceIds":["VSP_045211"],"isoformSequenceStatus":"Described"}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"1339277"}],"value":"Testis"}],"commentType":"TISSUE SPECIFICITY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenc